# tally 2.2.1, 221.8 (L §8.3 l.2270: a refusal "names its file, line and item, the values it names
# printed as §2.4 says"): LOAD-SAME for a same between an observed row and a planned instance names the
# keys as written, at the line of the same. A guard: both interpreters so.
=== options exit=1
=== t2218.tally
model t2218
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input bank: observed
move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, 10)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 100.00 PLN) "r1"
  same pay[2026-03] = bank[r1]
ask b: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SAME same pay[2026-03] = bank[r1]: an observed row and a planned instance of one model; state fulfils on the row (t2218.tally:22)
